findings.suggested_fix:
Add a checked/pressed rule sourced from tokens, e.g.
    QPushButton:checked, QPushButton:pressed {
        background-color: {t.accent};
        color: {t.bg};
        border-color: {t.accent};
    }
so engaged toggles (Open in RViz / Open in Rerun / Advanced) read as on.

Add a broad fallback after the teaching-error except, mirroring the record worker: `except Exception as exc:  # surface any parse/backend failure as text, not a crash
    if not worker.is_cancelled:
        self.app.call_from_thread(self._show_query_error, f"Query failed: {exc}")
    return`. (Alternatively add `exit_on_error=False` to the @work decorator, but the explicit fallback gives the user a teaching status line instead of a silent no-op.)
